IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sk-pit`

-- The Income Tax Act, 2000 (Saskatchewan) -- the individual taxpayer's questions, for the 2026 taxation year.
-- Every question calls the rules in sk-pit.l4; nothing is restated here. Plain inputs, one per fact the person can state.
-- Federal amounts (taxable income, net income, the CPP/EI and pension amounts, adjusted income) come from the person's
-- federal return; see the federal Income Tax Act encoding in subjects/ca/income-tax-act/.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: the Act is quoted from the King's Printer consolidation, (c) 2026, Government of Saskatchewan;
-- not an official version. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Must I pay Saskatchewan income tax`

@export Am I liable to pay Saskatchewan income tax under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 6(1), and under which clause?
GIVEN `I was resident in Saskatchewan on 31 December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the tax year (31 December, or the day you left Canada or died)
      `my income earned outside Saskatchewan` IS A NUMBER @desc Your income for the year earned outside Saskatchewan (for example business income from a permanent establishment in another province), in Canadian dollars; 0 if none
      `my income earned in Saskatchewan` IS A NUMBER @desc Your income for the year earned in Saskatchewan as the federal rules allocate it, in Canadian dollars (only needed if you were not resident on 31 December)
GIVETH A `Liability under s 6(1)`
`Am I liable to Saskatchewan tax` MEANS
    `the s 6(1) category` `I was resident in Saskatchewan on 31 December` `my income earned outside Saskatchewan` `my income earned in Saskatchewan`

§ `My Saskatchewan tax before credits`

@export How much Saskatchewan tax is imposed on my 2026 taxable income under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 8, before credits?
GIVEN `the taxation year` IS A NUMBER @desc The tax year, for example 2026 (only 2026 is covered)
      `I was resident in Saskatchewan on 31 December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the tax year
      `my income earned outside Saskatchewan` IS A NUMBER @desc Your income for the year earned outside Saskatchewan, in Canadian dollars; 0 if none
      `my income earned in Saskatchewan` IS A NUMBER @desc Your income for the year earned in Saskatchewan, in Canadian dollars (needed only if some income was earned outside Saskatchewan or you were not resident on 31 December)
      `my income for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net income for the year as on your federal return (line 23600), in Canadian dollars
      `my taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable income as on your federal return (line 26000), or taxable income earned in Canada if you were not resident in Canada, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much Saskatchewan tax before credits` MEANS
    LET `category` MEANS `the s 6(1) category` `I was resident in Saskatchewan on 31 December` `my income earned outside Saskatchewan` `my income earned in Saskatchewan`
    IN  IF NOT (`the taxation year is encoded` `the taxation year`)
        THEN `not covered` `only the 2026 taxation year is encoded`
        ELSE IF `category` EQUALS `not liable under s 6(1)`
             THEN `not covered` `the individual is not liable to tax under s 6(1): not resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year and no income earned in Saskatchewan`
             ELSE `answered` (`the s 8 tax for 2026` `category` `my taxable income` `my income earned in Saskatchewan` `my income for the year`)

§ `My non-refundable credits, 2026`

@export How much is my 2026 Saskatchewan basic personal credit under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 11(3)(b)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my basic personal credit` MEANS `the s 11 basic personal credit for 2026`

@export How much is my 2026 Saskatchewan spousal credit under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 12(3)(b)?
GIVEN `I claim the federal spouse or common-law partner amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to the federal spouse or common-law partner amount (Income Tax Act (Canada) s 118(1)(a)) for the year
      `my spouse's net income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your spouse's or common-law partner's net income for the year (or, if you separated because the relationship broke down, their income while you were together), in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my spousal credit` MEANS
    IF `I claim the federal spouse or common-law partner amount`
    THEN `the s 12 spousal credit for 2026` `my spouse's net income`
    ELSE 0

@export How much is my 2026 Saskatchewan equivalent-to-spouse (eligible dependant) credit under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 13(3)(b)?
GIVEN `I claim the federal eligible dependant amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to the federal amount for an eligible dependant (Income Tax Act (Canada) s 118(1)(b)) for this person
      `I claim the Saskatchewan spousal credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claim the Saskatchewan spousal credit this year (s 13 is only for those who do not)
      `the dependant's net income` IS A NUMBER @desc The net income for the year of the person you claim for, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my equivalent-to-spouse credit` MEANS
    IF `I claim the federal eligible dependant amount` AND (NOT `I claim the Saskatchewan spousal credit`)
    THEN `the s 13 equivalent-to-spouse credit for 2026` `the dependant's net income`
    ELSE 0

@export How much is my 2026 Saskatchewan age credit under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 17?
GIVEN `my age on 31 December` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age, in whole years, at the end of the tax year
      `my income for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net income for the year (federal line 23600), in Canadian dollars
      `the 2026 age amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The 2026 Saskatchewan age amount: the Act's $4,894 as indexed under s 51(3) for 2026 (shown on the Saskatchewan tax form SK428 or TD1SK), in Canadian dollars
      `the 2026 age income threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The 2026 income threshold for the age amount: the Act's $36,430 as indexed under s 51(3) for 2026 (shown on form SK428), in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my age credit` MEANS
    `the s 17 age credit` `my age on 31 December` `my income for the year` `the 2026 age amount` `the 2026 age income threshold`

@export How much is my Saskatchewan pension credit under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 18?
GIVEN `I was resident in Saskatchewan on 31 December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the tax year
      `my eligible pension income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pension income eligible for the federal pension income amount (Income Tax Act (Canada) s 118(3), the amount in paragraph (b) of B), in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my pension credit` MEANS
    `the s 18 pension credit` `I was resident in Saskatchewan on 31 December` `my eligible pension income`

@export May I claim the Saskatchewan dependent child credit, as between me and my cohabiting spouse, under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 19(1.1)?
GIVEN `I had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on 31 December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the last day of the year, you had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner (as the federal Canada child benefit rules define it)
      `my taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable income for the year, in Canadian dollars
      `my spouse's taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your cohabiting spouse's or partner's taxable income for the year, in Canadian dollars; 0 if none
      `my spouse renounces the credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your taxable incomes are exactly equal: whether your spouse or partner gives up their claim to the credit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I claim the dependent child credit` IF
    `s 19(1.1) lets me claim the dependent child credit` `I had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on 31 December` `my taxable income` `my spouse's taxable income` `my spouse renounces the credit`

@export How much is my 2026 Saskatchewan dependent child credit under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 19(4)(b)?
GIVEN `I was resident in Saskatchewan on 31 December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the tax year
      `I may claim as between me and my spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 19(1.1) lets you claim (see the question on claiming as between spouses; yes if you had no cohabiting spouse)
      `my children for the credit` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children lived with you on 31 December (or on the day they died) and were your qualified dependants for the Canada child benefit at some time in the year
      `of them, children I claim the equivalent-to-spouse credit for` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those children, how many you claim the Saskatchewan equivalent-to-spouse credit for (0 or 1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my dependent child credit` MEANS
    `the s 19 dependent child credit for 2026` `I was resident in Saskatchewan on 31 December` `I may claim as between me and my spouse` `my children for the credit` `of them, children I claim the equivalent-to-spouse credit for`

@export How much is my 2026 Saskatchewan senior supplementary credit under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 20?
GIVEN `I was resident in Saskatchewan on 31 December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the tax year (or, if you died in the year, on the date of death)
      `my age on 31 December` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age, in whole years, at the end of the tax year (or at death)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my senior supplementary credit` MEANS
    `the s 20 senior supplementary credit for 2026` `I was resident in Saskatchewan on 31 December` `my age on 31 December`

@export How much is my Saskatchewan charitable and other gifts credit under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 21?
GIVEN `my total gifts claimed` IS A NUMBER @desc The total gifts (charitable, cultural, ecological) you claim for the year, the same amount as on your federal return, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my gifts credit` MEANS `the s 21 gifts credit` `my total gifts claimed`

@export How much is my 2026 Saskatchewan mental or physical impairment (disability) credit under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 23?
GIVEN `I am eligible for the federal disability tax credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are eligible for the federal disability amount (Income Tax Act (Canada) s 118.3(1)), with an approved certificate
      `the 2026 disability amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The 2026 Saskatchewan disability amount: the 2025 figure of $13,986 as indexed under s 51(3) for 2026 (shown on form SK428), in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my impairment credit` MEANS
    `the s 23 impairment credit` `I am eligible for the federal disability tax credit` `the 2026 disability amount`

@export How much is my Saskatchewan EI premiums and CPP contributions credit under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 28?
GIVEN `my CPP base contributions and EI premiums` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your Canada Pension Plan base contributions and Employment Insurance premiums that the federal credit (Income Tax Act (Canada) s 118.7) counts, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my EI and CPP credit` MEANS `the s 28 EI and CPP credit` `my CPP base contributions and EI premiums`

§ `My Saskatchewan tax after credits`

@export How much Saskatchewan income tax do I owe for 2026 after the non-refundable credits of The Income Tax Act, 2000?
GIVEN `the taxation year` IS A NUMBER @desc The tax year, for example 2026 (only 2026 is covered)
      `I am a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the taxpayer is a trust or estate (not covered)
      `I am exempt from federal tax under s 149(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are exempt from federal income tax under Income Tax Act (Canada) s 149(1) for the period (for example as a foreign diplomat); not covered
      `I was resident in Saskatchewan on 31 December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the tax year
      `my income earned outside Saskatchewan` IS A NUMBER @desc Your income for the year earned outside Saskatchewan, in Canadian dollars; 0 if none
      `my income earned in Saskatchewan` IS A NUMBER @desc Your income for the year earned in Saskatchewan, in Canadian dollars
      `my income for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net income for the year (federal line 23600), in Canadian dollars
      `my taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable income (federal line 26000), in Canadian dollars
      `my spousal credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Saskatchewan spousal credit (see that question), in Canadian dollars; 0 if none
      `my equivalent-to-spouse credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Saskatchewan equivalent-to-spouse credit (see that question); 0 if none
      `my age credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Saskatchewan age credit (see that question); 0 if none
      `my pension credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Saskatchewan pension credit (see that question); 0 if none
      `my dependent child credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Saskatchewan dependent child credit (see that question); 0 if none
      `my senior supplementary credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Saskatchewan senior supplementary credit (see that question); 0 if none
      `my gifts credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Saskatchewan gifts credit (see that question); 0 if none
      `my impairment credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Saskatchewan impairment credit (see that question); 0 if none
      `my EI and CPP credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Saskatchewan EI and CPP credit (see that question); 0 if none
      `my other Saskatchewan credits` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other Saskatchewan non-refundable credits you claim (for example medical expenses, tuition, caregiver, dividend tax credit), as already computed, in Canadian dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much Saskatchewan tax do I owe after credits` MEANS
    `the Saskatchewan tax after non-refundable credits` `the taxation year` `I am a trust` `I am exempt from federal tax under s 149(1)`
        (`the s 6(1) category` `I was resident in Saskatchewan on 31 December` `my income earned outside Saskatchewan` `my income earned in Saskatchewan`)
        `my taxable income` `my income earned in Saskatchewan` `my income for the year`
        (`Division 2 credits for 2026` WITH
            `s 11 basic personal`       IS `the s 11 basic personal credit for 2026`
            `s 12 spousal`              IS `my spousal credit`
            `s 13 equivalent-to-spouse` IS `my equivalent-to-spouse credit`
            `s 17 age`                  IS `my age credit`
            `s 18 pension`              IS `my pension credit`
            `s 19 dependent child`      IS `my dependent child credit`
            `s 20 senior supplementary` IS `my senior supplementary credit`
            `s 21 gifts`                IS `my gifts credit`
            `s 23 impairment`           IS `my impairment credit`
            `s 28 EI and CPP`           IS `my EI and CPP credit`
            `other credits not encoded` IS `my other Saskatchewan credits`)

§ `My low-income tax credit`

@export How much Saskatchewan low-income tax credit will be paid to me in each quarter for the 2026 taxation year, under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 39 and the Low-income Tax Credit Regulations?
GIVEN `I am an eligible individual for the GST/HST credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an eligible individual for the federal GST/HST credit (Income Tax Act (Canada) s 122.5(1)): resident in Canada and 19 or older, or with a spouse or partner, or a parent living with your child
      `I filed my 2026 return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have filed your income tax return for 2026
      `I have a cohabiting spouse or partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner (your qualified relation) at the start of the payment month
      `I claim the eligible dependant amount for a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have no spouse or partner and claim the federal amount for an eligible dependant for one of your children
      `my number of qualified dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children under 19 live with you and depend on you (your qualified dependants for the GST/HST credit)
      `of them, children in shared custody` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those children, how many live with you and another parent on a roughly equal basis (shared custody); 0 if none
      `my adjusted family net income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net income for 2026 plus your cohabiting spouse's or partner's, in Canadian dollars
      `the 2026 child amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The 2026 Saskatchewan low-income tax credit amount for a child (the s 39(5.2)(c)(iv)(A) amount, indexed; published by the CRA), in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much low-income tax credit each quarter` MEANS
    `the s 39 low-income tax credit for each specified month` `I am an eligible individual for the GST/HST credit` `I filed my 2026 return` `I have a cohabiting spouse or partner` `I claim the eligible dependant amount for a child` `my number of qualified dependants` `of them, children in shared custody` `my adjusted family net income` `the 2026 child amount`

@export When will my Saskatchewan low-income tax credit for a taxation year be paid, and how much each time, under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 39(7)-(9)?
GIVEN `the taxation year` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxation year the credit is for, for example 2026
      `my quarterly amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your quarterly low-income tax credit for that year (see the quarterly question), in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A LIST OF `Payment`
`When will my low-income tax credit be paid` MEANS `the s 39 payments` `the taxation year` `my quarterly amount`

§ `Filing, paying, and my refund`

@export Must I file a Saskatchewan income tax return for the year (The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 75 with federal s 150, and s 39(3)(b))?
GIVEN `I have Saskatchewan or federal tax payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have income tax payable for the year
      `I want the low-income tax credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you want to receive the Saskatchewan low-income tax credit (it is paid only if you file)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I file a return` IF `I have Saskatchewan or federal tax payable` OR `I want the low-income tax credit`

@export Can my Saskatchewan low-income tax credit refund be taken by a creditor, under The Income Tax Act, 2000 s 40?
GIVEN `the CRA applies it to another amount I owe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the refund is being applied by the Canada Revenue Agency against another debt you owe to the government (federal Income Tax Act s 164(2))
      `it is garnished for family support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the refund is being garnished for child or spousal support under the federal Family Orders and Agreements Enforcement Assistance Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my low-income tax credit refund be taken` IF
    `s 40(2) lets the refund be taken` `the CRA applies it to another amount I owe` `it is garnished for family support`
